===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:privat<alt:privat(e)><ety:der<la:prīvātus>>}}
From {{inh|en|enm|privat|alt=privat(e)|t=individual, exclusive, private}}, from {{der|en|la|prīvātus||bereaved, deprived, set apart from, release}}, {{glossary|perfect}} {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|prīvō||to bereave, deprive, release}} (see {{af|en|-ate|id1=adjective|pos1=adjective-forming suffix}} for more), from {{m|la|prīvus||private, one's own, proper}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*per}}; compare {{m|en|prime}}, {{m|en|prior}}, {{m|en|pristine}}. {{doublet|en|privy}}.

